+// A1-16: a lock is one unsigned int: 0 = free, 1 = held.
+// __sync_lock_test_and_set(lock, 1) writes 1 and returns the OLD value in ONE indivisible
+// step: "was it free? then it is mine now". With a normal "if (*lock == 0) *lock = 1;" two
+// threads can both see 0 (a timer interrupt between the check and the write) and both enter.
+// While we wait we give the CPU away (sched_yield) - the holder needs it to unlock.
+
 /**
